WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS LICENSED DIFFERENTLY FROM THE CODE

The code is MIT: take it, run it, sell something built on it, no strings. The
point of an audit tool is that people run it.

The register is a claim about what is true, and a claim that travels without its
source becomes a rumour. Attribution is not a toll here — it is the mechanism by
which a corrected entry reaches everyone who repeated it. This register has been
publicly wrong four times in three days: four entries were expelled from the
passing column on 2026-08-12 when their cited tools turned out to be zero-star
repositories and one could not be found at all, and an erratum written on
2026-08-11 was itself wrong, calling a price rise urgent one day after it had
been cancelled. Every one of those corrections is published and dated. That
discipline only means anything if the people quoting a verdict can be found
again when it changes.
